From df919c8ddc2b2cbe4deeabbe7ea1934918ddc47b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Frdlik <michaelf.ms@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 14:12:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Thylacine CL-3: a real Triple::Thylacine + clang
 ToolChain + lld default

Add a first-class aarch64-thylacine target to the LLVM/clang driver so that
`clang --target=aarch64-thylacine` drives the ELF link directly, fixing the
root cause the pouch-clang/pouch-ld wrappers work around: an unknown OS falls
to Generic_ELF, whose buildLinker shells out to the host Darwin toolchain and
emits Mach-O linker arguments the ELF ld.lld rejects.

- llvm/TargetParser: a Triple::Thylacine OSType (+ isOSThylacine, getOSTypeName,
  parseOS, LastOSType retargeted).
- clang Driver: a Fuchsia-templated toolchains::Thylacine -- static, non-PIE
  (kernel/elf.c rejects ET_DYN/PT_DYNAMIC), libc++ + compiler-rt builtins over
  the musl (pouch) sysroot, ld.lld the ELF linker. Its Linker::ConstructJob
  reproduces tools/pouch-ld: crt1/crti before the inputs, the C++ runtime
  (libc++/libc++abi/libunwind) grouped, then musl + builtins grouped, crtn
  last; the libc++ headers resolved flat at include/c++/v1.
- clang Basic: a ThylacineTargetInfo predefining __unix__ (libc++ keys on it),
  __thylacine__, _REENTRANT, _GNU_SOURCE -- which also closes the CL-2 audit
  F2b split-personality seam (the OS macro is now automatic for the runtime
  AND every consumer at once).

Verified against the pouch sysroot (clang built Release/AArch64):
- `-dumpmachine` -> aarch64-unknown-thylacine.
- The C link line matches tools/pouch-ld (ld.lld, -static, the three -z flags,
  --build-id=none, crt1/crti, -L, --start-group -lc <builtins> --end-group,
  crtn), plus --eh-frame-hdr; NO Darwin ld64 / -arch / platform_version.
- The C++ link additionally emits --start-group -lc++ -lc++abi -lunwind
  --end-group.
- Real C and C++ links produce valid static ET_EXEC (0 PT_DYNAMIC), the segment
  layout identical to pouch-ld modulo a benign PT_GNU_EH_FRAME the CL-2 C++
  binaries already carry.

The build.sh/CMake switchover to retire the wrappers, the CL-2 build_libcxx
re-point (drop the surgical -D__linux__ now that __thylacine__ is automatic),
and the in-guest boot proof land in CL-3b.

